  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Almost one in five litres of England's tap water leaks away before it reaches a tap.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "ALMOST *1 IN 5",
        "LITRES *LEAK",
        "BEFORE YOUR *TAP"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · ENVIRONMENT AGENCY",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "18.6",
            "suffix": "%",
            "l": "OF SUPPLY LOST TO LEAKS",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ENVIRONMENT AGENCY 2025–26"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "That's from the Environment Agency's new report.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "ENVIRONMENT *AGENCY",
        "NEW *REPORT"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "card",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · ENVIRONMENT AGENCY",
        "l1": "WATER RESOURCES",
        "l2": "2025 TO 2026",
        "source": "GOV.UK · 29 OCT 2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In total, two thousand six hundred and twenty-one million litres leaked every single day.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*2,621 MILLION",
        "*LITRES",
        "EVERY *DAY"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · ENVIRONMENT AGENCY",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "2,621",
            "static": true,
            "l": "MILLION LITRES A DAY · ENGLAND",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "source": "ENVIRONMENT AGENCY 2025–26"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "That's about a hundred and one litres for every home, every day.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "*101 LITRES",
        "EVERY *HOME",
        "EVERY *DAY"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "icon",
        "icon": "drop",
        "value": "101 L",
        "unit": "PER PROPERTY · PER DAY"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Essex and Suffolk Water lost eleven per cent. Thames Water, twenty-two point four.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "ESSEX & SUFFOLK *11%",
        "THAMES WATER *22.4%"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
        "tag": "OFFICIAL · ENVIRONMENT AGENCY",
        "items": [
          {
            "v": "11.0",
            "suffix": "%",
            "l": "ESSEX & SUFFOLK"
          },
          {
            "v": "22.4",
            "suffix": "%",
            "l": "THAMES WATER",
            "red": true
          }
        ],
        "bars": true,
        "source": "ENVIRONMENT AGENCY 2025–26"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The good news? Leakage is down about twelve per cent since twenty seventeen.",
      "gap": 0.3,
      "caps": [
        "THE *GOOD NEWS",
        "DOWN ABOUT *12%",
        "SINCE *2017"
      ],
      "scene": {
        "type": "stat",
